{"lines":[{"h":0.008720930389296444,"t":"1718867188","x":0.7716049391467531,"w":0.069958845774332645,"y":0.046511627815394085,"c":0.5},{"y":0.097383720784155137,"t":"demolishing buildings. Originally scheduled to be completed in 21 months, the construction of","x":0.10082305647853795,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"w":0.7592592366536457},{"h":0.017562816224474531,"y":0.11288218127896121,"x":0.10282682679832239,"t":"the underground line took three years. It was built just below street level using a technique known","w":0.77788085937499996,"c":1},{"t":"as 'cut and cover. A trench about ten metres wide and six metres deep was dug, and the sides","y":0.13074204923271338,"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.74691360473632817,"c":1,"x":0.10288064608741214},{"t":"temporarily held up with timber beams. Brick walls were then constructed, and finally a brick","w":0.74691360473632806,"x":0.098765419760322479,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.14811542992830451},{"t":"arch was added to create a tunnel. A two-metre-deep layer of soil was laid on top of the tunnel","w":0.74897120157877606,"x":0.10288065456897963,"y":0.16424418590075585,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"t":"and the road above rebuilt.","w":0.21604937235514321,"h":0.013083107479890832,"x":0.10082305033582926,"c":1,"y":0.18168433448974253},{"x":0.10082303482852373,"c":1,"t":"The Metropolitan line, which opened on 10 January 1863, was the world's first underground","h":0.016019188192342826,"y":0.21366279055120241,"w":0.73456792195638021},{"x":0.098765426347261973,"w":0.70370371500651041,"c":1,"t":"railway. On its first day, almost 40,000 passengers were carried between Paddington and","y":0.23110465101671318,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"h":0.017479524174343175,"w":0.75514404296874993,"t":"Farringdon, the journey taking about 18 minutes. By the end of the Metropolitan's first year of","x":0.1008230370135675,"y":0.24705535896726116,"c":1},{"y":0.26208252143655497,"x":0.10068873449285709,"c":1,"h":0.018854415318429574,"w":0.38087847391764323,"t":"operation, 9.5 million journeys had been made."},{"x":0.10082305550755194,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1,"w":0.76543207804361968,"t":"Even as the Metropolitan began operation, the first extensions to the line were being authorised;","y":0.29651162774746997},{"t":"these were built over the next five years, reaching Moorgate in the east of London and","h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"x":0.10288064734511702,"w":0.68312759399414058,"y":0.31389870421240951},{"t":"Hammersmith in the west. The original plan was to pull the trains with steam locomotives, using","y":0.32979976453061943,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.10082304643661463,"c":1,"w":0.76954732259114589},{"t":"firebricks in the boilers to provide steam, but these engines were never introduced. Instead, the","x":0.1007629704492092,"y":0.34544226435092806,"c":1,"w":0.7532023620605468,"h":0.017606187063336165},{"c":1,"w":0.76131688435872402,"t":"line used specially designed locomotives that were fitted with water tanks in which steam could","x":0.10082303921654888,"h":0.015991796172268979,"y":0.36336866908514909},{"t":"be condensed. However, smoke and fumes remained a problem, even though ventilation shafts","c":1,"y":0.380742049219575,"x":0.10082305740817323,"h":0.016195524146054296,"w":0.75308639526367194},{"x":0.10277483953106838,"y":0.39537942011257088,"t":"were added to the tunnels.","h":0.014564233337330479,"c":1,"w":0.21017172495524089},{"t":"Despite the extension of the underground railway, by the 1880s, congestion on London's streets","y":0.43021201411875443,"w":0.75925923665364581,"h":0.016008916255020766,"c":1,"x":0.10082305645412039},{"t":"had become worse. The problem was partly that the existing underground lines formed a circuit","x":0.098765442354384253,"y":0.44611307446383996,"w":0.7654320780436199,"h":0.016195524146054296,"c":1},{"h":0.014546867815428799,"c":1,"x":0.10082304830199131,"t":"around the centre of London and extended to the suburbs, but did not cross the capital's centre.","w":0.75720163981119804,"y":0.46366279056475213},{"w":0.77172938028971361,"h":0.017853525698676376,"x":0.10076166211182293,"t":"The 'cut and cover' method of construction was not an option in this part of the capital. The only","y":0.47781573811657962,"c":1},{"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"y":0.49705535917685162,"t":"alternative was to tunnel deep underground.","w":0.34979423522949216,"x":0.10288066006078225},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.7654320780436199,"x":0.10082305555168347,"t":"Although the technology to create these tunnels existed, steam locomotives could not be used in","y":0.52906976729539823,"c":1},{"w":0.78189300537109374,"h":0.01599350750656936,"t":"such a confined space. It wasn't until the development of a reliable electric motor, and a means of","c":1,"x":0.098765432911160925,"y":0.54505300350351404},{"c":1,"t":"transferring power from the generator to a moving train, that the world's first deep-level electric","y":0.56242638384832333,"w":0.7592592366536457,"x":0.10288066963519905,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"t":"railway, the City & South London, became possible. The line opened in 1890, and ran from the","x":0.098765443412595078,"h":0.016034596379148724,"y":0.57848837193982949,"w":0.75925923665364581,"c":1},{"y":0.59593023242550558,"t":"City to Stockwell, south of the River Thames. The trains were made up of three carriages and","w":0.74279836018880208,"x":0.10082304202522627,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"y":0.61189634874798804,"t":"driven by electric engines. The carriages were narrow and had tiny windows just below the roof","x":0.10288065236824195,"w":0.76131688435872391,"c":1,"h":0.014557139752750747},{"t":"because it was thought that passengers would not want to look out at the tunnel walls. The line","y":0.62773893260400448,"w":0.75320048014322916,"h":0.017473598812718816,"c":1,"x":0.10076026306938048},{"x":0.10082304643357039,"w":0.76954732259114578,"c":1,"t":"was not without its problems, mainly caused by an unreliable power supply. Although the City &","h":0.016017476296396715,"y":0.64534883706320323},{"t":"South London Railway was a great technical achievement, it did not make a profit. Then, in 1900,","w":0.78189300537109385,"y":0.66133720914296834,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1,"x":0.10082304454810649},{"t":"the Central London Railway, known as theTuppenny Tube', began operation using new electric","y":0.67726737323215203,"w":0.76748967488606779,"x":0.10082306549935301,"h":0.017500068048987183,"c":1},{"x":0.10082303731290096,"y":0.69611307392886301,"w":0.77366256713867188,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"t":"locomotives. It was very popular and soon afterwards new railways and extensions were added to"},{"y":0.71075581414037248,"w":0.72633743286132812,"h":0.017453844050215328,"t":"the growing tube network. By 1907, the heart of today's Underground system was in place.","c":1,"x":0.10082305483991207},{"y":0.8677325579865931,"w":0.024691357612609766,"x":0.85802469146118487,"h":0.011627907185728592,"t":"17","c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.95314993796778535,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","w":0.30612678527832038,"x":0.66991655033568553,"h":0.03375352650564889}],"w":2400,"h":3395}